Purpose: Restrict the upstream build script to the Linux target family (Plan 0003, Locked Decision 1). Every darwin and win32 entry is deleted from the target list, together with the code that existed only for them: the win32-to-windows name mapping, the Windows bunfs root, the compile windows options, the macOS re-signing step, and the zip form of the script's own release packaging. The --android mode of patch 0001 is untouched; a default build now produces Linux targets only.
Upstream files: packages/opencode/script/build.ts
Rebase note: Check the target list first; upstream adds targets there. The --android ternary and the tarball condition come from patch 0001 and must survive the rebase.

